    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290-a2">

                <pb facs="0628" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg544"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    89.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fouchard to Mr. Roumain.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Hayti,<lb/>Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 6, 1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Fellow-Citizen</hi>: I have the advantage of
                    placing before your eyes a passage extracted from a letter that Mr. Bassett,
                    Haytian consul at New York, addressed to me, relative to kerosene oil.</p>
                <p>I would be thankful to you, my dear fellow-citizen, if you would settle for me
                    the question of at what degree must the oil permitted to enter this country be
                    without violating the law which prohibits the importation of such oils. I await
                    your information to give instructions on this subject to the Haytian consul at
                    New York.</p>
                <p>Please accept, my dear fellow-citizen, the assurance of my highest
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>C. FOUCHARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
